{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"4f70444e976714f1","name":"card_event_ijn_shirakumo","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Homefront/events/card_event_ijn_shirakumo","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"IJN SHIRAKUMO","text":"Pin target unit. If it is already pinned, remove it instead. Your HQ gains +2 defense.","flavorText":"Commissioned in 1928, Shirakumo was part of the Fubuki-class, a revolutionary class of Japanese destroyers which set new standards in firepower and speed. Assigned to Destroyer Division 12, she was active from the beginning of Japan’s war in China and supported landings in southern China and French Indochina. At the start of WWII, Shirakumo escorted invasion convoys to Malaya and British Borneo. In February 1942, she helped sink the British cable-laying ship Anking. Later that month, she took part in the Battle of Sunda Strait, where Japanese forces sank the Allied cruisers Perth and Houston, as well as the Dutch destroyer Evertsen. During the Guadalcanal campaign, Shirakumo ran Tokyo Express missions to reinforce Japanese positions. On 28 August 1942, a bomb hit her engine room during an air attack, putting her out of action until October. She resumed escort duties in Northern-Pacific waters in 1943 but was lost with all hands on 16 March 1944 when the submarine USS Harder torpedoed her off Hokkaido while she was escorting a convoy to the Kuril islands.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["subtype.navy"],"Name":"card_event_ijn_shirakumo","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_ijn_shirakumo_title","SourceString":"IJN SHIRAKUMO","LocalizedString":"IJN SHIRAKUMO"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_ijn_shirakumo_text","SourceString":"Pin target unit. If it is already pinned, remove it instead. Your HQ gains +2 defense.","LocalizedString":"Pin target unit. If it is already pinned, remove it instead. Your HQ gains +2 defense."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_ijn_shirakumo_history","SourceString":"Commissioned in 1928, Shirakumo was part of the Fubuki-class, a revolutionary class of Japanese destroyers which set new standards in firepower and speed. Assigned to Destroyer Division 12, she was active from the beginning of Japan’s war in China and supported landings in southern China and French Indochina. At the start of WWII, Shirakumo escorted invasion convoys to Malaya and British Borneo. In February 1942, she helped sink the British cable-laying ship Anking. Later that month, she took part in the Battle of Sunda Strait, where Japanese forces sank the Allied cruisers Perth and Houston, as well as the Dutch destroyer Evertsen. During the Guadalcanal campaign, Shirakumo ran Tokyo Express missions to reinforce Japanese positions. On 28 August 1942, a bomb hit her engine room during an air attack, putting her out of action until October. She resumed escort duties in Northern-Pacific waters in 1943 but was lost with all hands on 16 March 1944 when the submarine USS Harder torpedoed her off Hokkaido while she was escorting a convoy to the Kuril islands.","LocalizedString":"Commissioned in 1928, Shirakumo was part of the Fubuki-class, a revolutionary class of Japanese destroyers which set new standards in firepower and speed. Assigned to Destroyer Division 12, she was active from the beginning of Japan’s war in China and supported landings in southern China and French Indochina. At the start of WWII, Shirakumo escorted invasion convoys to Malaya and British Borneo. In February 1942, she helped sink the British cable-laying ship Anking. Later that month, she took part in the Battle of Sunda Strait, where Japanese forces sank the Allied cruisers Perth and Houston, as well as the Dutch destroyer Evertsen. During the Guadalcanal campaign, Shirakumo ran Tokyo Express missions to reinforce Japanese positions. On 28 August 1942, a bomb hit her engine room during an air attack, putting her out of action until October. She resumed escort duties in Northern-Pacific waters in 1943 but was lost with all hands on 16 March 1944 when the submarine USS Harder torpedoed her off Hokkaido while she was escorting a convoy to the Kuril islands."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/10_Homefront/T_ijn_shirakumo.T_ijn_shirakumo","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/IJN_SHIRAKUMO.IJN_SHIRAKUMO","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":282.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_ijn_shirakumo_photo","SourceString":"Japanese Navy destroyer Shirakumo in 1931.","LocalizedString":"Japanese Navy destroyer Shirakumo in 1931."},"isDraw":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"TempDeck","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"},{"name":"TempCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"PreviousIndex","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"nonJpnFound","type":"bool","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_ijn_shirakumo_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":true,"flags":"FUNC_Event | FUNC_Public | FUNC_HasOutParms | FUNC_BlueprintCallable | FUNC_BlueprintEvent","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarge